## Root cause (read-only src/ inspection — NO fix, FREEZE respected)
input.rs:554-556 — the `_ =>` catch-all in `LibinputProvider::poll()` pushes
`InputEvent::Activity` for ANY event that is not Device/Keyboard(Fn)/Touch/Switch
(pointer motion, gestures, etc. from seat0 `main_input`).

main.rs:875-884 maps `InputEvent::Activity` → `input.notify_activity()` (no-op) +
`backlight.notify_activity()` (backlight.rs:253-255) → resets `last_active = now()`.

On an ACTIVE laptop session with trackpad/pointer motion, seat0 generates a
continuous stream of pointer events → `last_active` resets ~every 10ms loop tick
→ `compute_target()` (backlight.rs:176-196) always selects the ACTIVE branch
(since < 30_000ms) → brightness stays at the display-linked level
`display_to_touchbar(90, 128) = 54`. The 60s idle decay (→ DIMMED=1 at 30s, → 0
at 60s) never triggers because the bar is never idle while the operator is active.

This is CORRECT adaptive behavior — the oracle ports the same process_event wake
at backup_old/tiny-dfr-mbp142/src/backlight.rs:102-118 (wakes on
Keyboard/Pointer/Gesture/Touch + lid-open).

## Verdict 4c
NOT an abort. The bar holding at 54 is the EXPECTED adaptive-lit state under an
active operator session. The "decay to 0" check is only observable on a TRULY
idle session (no trackpad/pointer motion for >60s) — not exercisable here. The
A/B test's decisive signal (content vs backlight) does NOT depend on 4c.

## Finding (ADR candidate — logged, NOT fixed)
The idle-decay path (Stage-4 acceptance item — the DIM/OFF schedule) cannot be
exercised under an active operator session because seat0 pointer activity keeps
the bar awake. This is a TESTABILITY gap, not a defect: the oracle has the same
behavior. To exercise idle decay in a future session, the operator must stop all
trackpad/pointer input for >60s (or test under a headless/no-seat0 condition).
Candidate ADR: document the active-session idle-decay testability caveat and
scope idle-decay verification to a no-input condition.